{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Fix re-derived on current origin/main (1ab859777a) — implemented, gates green\n\nPhase 1 re-confirmed deterministically on current main before touching code: two worktree\nviews of one store (`.tickets-tracker` symlinked to the canonical store, real per-worktree\n`.rebar`, exactly as `make worktree` provisions) derived two DISTINCT `enrich-drain.lock`\npaths and BOTH `_acquire_advisory_lock` calls succeeded simultaneously; the canonical\n`.rebar` stayed empty. `_gate_marker_path` showed the same split for `enrich-gate.json`.\nCounter-verified post-fix with the same harness: one lock path, second acquire refused,\nlock lands in the canonical `.rebar`.\n\nFix follows intangible-ladyish-vicuna's landed shape (dae7f62696, 93a9-66cf-e681-4f49) at the\ntwo sites vicuna's report named as this ticket's remainder:\n\n* `llm/enrich_drain.py` — new `_canonical_tracker` delegating to\n  `_store.lock.canonical_tracker` (lazy, never-raising); `_rebar_dir` now derives from the\n  resolved path, so the drain lock AND drain log are keyed on the store and no caller can\n  defeat it (covers the `rebar enrich` CLI entry the RCA flagged). `_spawn_detached_drain`\n  hands the child `_canonical_tracker(tracker)` as argv[1], so a detached child never holds\n  a tracker path that dies with the worktree (AC3).\n* `llm/overlap/queue.py` — `_gate_marker_path` derives from the same resolved path\n  (lazy import of enrich_drain's helper; no import cycle — enrich_drain imports queue only\n  inside functions).\n\nRED→GREEN: 6 new tests mirroring vicuna's (path invariance across two worktree views, real\nlock contention across worktrees, lock lands on the canonical store not the worktree,\ndetached-child argv is canonical, gate-marker path invariance, cross-worktree marker\ninvalidation) — all observed failing on the pre-fix tree for the pinned mechanism, all green\npost-fix. `make lint` (incl. complexity ratchet), `make typecheck`, and the full\nenrich/queue/compact_trigger/doctor_locks test files pass. Proceeding to Gerrit."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787333809891006001,"uuid":"78b4749d-6882-4f36-9b37-376a4ac8b8b7"}